sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: The square on a second apotome of a medial straight line applied to a rational straight line produces as breadth a third apotome.
----
proof:

Let {AB} be a second apotome of a medial straight line, and {CD} rational, and to {CD} let there be applied {CE} equal to the square on {AB} producing {CF} as breadth.

I say that {CF} is a third apotome.

Let {BG} be the annex to {AB}, therefore {AG} and {GB} are medial straight lines commensurable in square only which contains a medial rectangle. [!just X.75]

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="370" height="170" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.99 diagram" src="propX99.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure: the second apotome of a medial AB with its annex BG on
    // the line AG, the rational CD, CE (DCFE) equal to the square on AB
    // applied to CD with breadth CF, CH equal to the square on AG (DCFE with
    // FKHE), KL (HKML) equal to the square on BG, FM bisected at N and the
    // parallel NO.
    // Added, all hidden at rest: solid twins AB and BG (initiallyHidden) so
    // AB stands alone and the annex is produced from B to G; transparent
    // targets CF, CK, KH, KM, CM, FM, MN, EF (;0;0;0); faceless rectangles
    // CE, CH, KL, CL, FL, FO, NL (;0;0;0;0) for the areas the text names,
    // since the random-faced originals would be raised over the figure when
    // lit (#140). No angle is called right.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, B, C, D, G (line sliders)
    // and the offscreen frees. C and D arrive with "CD rational", G with the
    // annex, so all three are deferred. F, E, K, H, M, L, N, O are derived
    // and listed per slide.
    var GIVEN = ["A","B","AB"];
    var RAT   = GIVEN.concat(["C","D","CD"]);
    var APPL  = RAT.concat(["F","E","DCFE","CE","CF"]);
    var ANNEX = APPL.concat(["G","BG"]);
    var GA    = ANNEX.concat(["AG"]);
    var CHS   = GA.concat(["K","H","FKHE","CH","CK"]);
    var KLS   = CHS.concat(["M","L","HKML","KL","KM","KH","CL","CM","FL","FM"]);
    var ALL   = KLS.concat(["N","O","NO","FO","NL","MN","EF"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "X.99",
        elements: [
            "A0;point;free;-1000,40;0;0",
            "A3;point;free;1000,40;0;0",
            "C0;point;free;40,-1000;0;0",
            "C3;point;free;40,1000;0;0",
            "A;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,120,0",
            "B;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,190,0",
            "C;point;lineSlider;C0,C3,0,70",
            "D;point;lineSlider;C0,C3,0,140",
            "CD;line;connect;C,D",
            "F';point;parallelogram;C,A0,A3;0;0",
            "F;point;proportion;C,D,A,B,A,B,C,F'",
            "E;point;parallelogram;D,C,F",
            "DCFE;polygon;quadrilateral;D,C,F,E;0;0;black;random",
            "G;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,250,0",
            "AG;line;connect;A,G",
            "K;point;proportion;C,D,A,G,A,G,C,F'",
            "H;point;parallelogram;D,C,K",
            "FKHE;polygon;quadrilateral;F,K,H,E;0;0;black;random",
            "M;point;proportion;C,D,B,G,B,G,K,F'",
            "L;point;parallelogram;D,C,M",
            "HKML;polygon;quadrilateral;H,K,M,L;0;0;black;random",
            "N;point;midpoint;F,M",
            "O;point;parallelogram;D,C,N",
            "NO;line;connect;N,O",
            // Slide-only twins and highlight targets.
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "BG;line;connect;B,G",
            "CF;line;connect;C,F;0;0;0",
            "CK;line;connect;C,K;0;0;0",
            "KH;line;connect;K,H;0;0;0",
            "KM;line;connect;K,M;0;0;0",
            "CM;line;connect;C,M;0;0;0",
            "FM;line;connect;F,M;0;0;0",
            "MN;line;connect;M,N;0;0;0",
            "EF;line;connect;E,F;0;0;0",
            "CE;polygon;quadrilateral;C,F,E,D;0;0;0;0",
            "CH;polygon;quadrilateral;C,K,H,D;0;0;0;0",
            "KL;polygon;quadrilateral;K,M,L,H;0;0;0;0",
            "CL;polygon;quadrilateral;C,M,L,D;0;0;0;0",
            "FL;polygon;quadrilateral;F,M,L,E;0;0;0;0",
            "FO;polygon;quadrilateral;F,N,O,E;0;0;0;0",
            "NL;polygon;quadrilateral;N,M,L,O;0;0;0;0"
        ],
        initiallyHidden: ["AB","BG"],
        deferDraggables: ["C","D","G"],
        aliases: { "GB": "BG", "LF": "FL", "MF": "FM", "NM": "MN", "FE": "EF" },
        slides: [
            { text: "“The square on a second apotome of a medial straight line applied to a rational straight line",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB", "CD", "CE"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "X.99" }] },
            { text: "produces as breadth a third apotome.”",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CF"] },
            { text: "Let {AB} be a second apotome of a medial straight line,",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB"] },
            { text: "and {CD} rational,",
              visible: RAT,
              highlighted: ["CD"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "C", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "D", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "CD", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "and to {CD} let there be applied {CE} equal to the square on {AB}",
              visible: APPL,
              highlighted: ["CD", "AB"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "DCFE", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "producing {CF} as breadth.",
              visible: APPL,
              highlighted: ["CF"] },
            { text: "I say that {CF} is a third apotome.",
              visible: APPL,
              highlighted: ["CF"] },
            { text: "Let {BG} be the annex to {AB},",
              visible: ANNEX,
              highlighted: ["BG"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "BG", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeExtend },
                  { elem: "G", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "therefore {AG} and {GB} are medial straight lines commensurable in square only which contains a medial rectangle.",
              visible: GA,
              highlighted: ["AG", "BG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AB a second apotome of a medial", ref: "X.75" }] },
            { text: "Apply {CH}, equal to the square on {AG}, to {CD} producing {CK} as breadth,",
              visible: CHS,
              highlighted: ["AG", "CD", "CK"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "K", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "FKHE", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "and apply {KL}, equal to the square on {BG}, to {KH} producing {KM} as breadth.",
              visible: KLS,
              highlighted: ["BG", "KH", "KM"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "M", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "HKML", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "Then the whole {CL} equals the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB}.",
              visible: KLS,
              highlighted: ["CL", "AG", "BG"] },
            { text: "Therefore {CL} is also medial.",
              visible: KLS,
              highlighted: ["CL"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "sum of squares medial", ref: "X.15" }, { ref: "X.23.Cor" }] },
            { text: "And it is applied to the rational straight line {CD} producing {CM} as breadth,",
              visible: KLS,
              highlighted: ["CL", "CD", "CM"] },
            { text: "therefore {CM} is rational and incommensurable in length with {CD}.",
              visible: KLS,
              highlighted: ["CM", "CD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CM rational, incommensurable with CD", ref: "X.22" }] },
            { text: "Now, since the whole {CL} equals the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB},",
              visible: KLS,
              highlighted: ["CL", "AG", "BG"] },
            { text: "and, in these, {CE} equals the square on {AB},",
              visible: KLS,
              highlighted: ["CE", "AB"] },
            { text: "therefore the remainder {LF} equals twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB}.",
              visible: KLS,
              highlighted: ["FL", "AG", "BG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "LF = twice AG by GB", ref: "II.7" }] },
            { text: "Bisect {FM} at the point {N}, and draw {NO} parallel to {CD}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FM", "CD"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "N", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "NO", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "Then each of the rectangles {FO} and {NL} equals the rectangle {AG} by {GB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FO", "NL", "AG", "BG"] },
            { text: "But the rectangle {AG} by {GB} is medial, therefore {FL} is also medial.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AG", "BG", "FL"] },
            { text: "And it is applied to the rational straight line {EF} producing {FM} as breadth,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FL", "EF", "FM"] },
            { text: "therefore {FM} is also rational and incommensurable in length with {CD}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FM", "CD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "FM rational, incommensurable with CD", ref: "X.22" }] },
            { text: "Since {AG} and {GB} are commensurable in square only, therefore {AG} is incommensurable in length with {GB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AG", "BG"] },
            { text: "Therefore the square on {AG} is also incommensurable with the rectangle {AG} by {GB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AG", "BG"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "VI.1" }, { claim: "square incommensurable with rectangle", ref: "X.11" }] },
            { text: "But the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB} is commensurable with the square on {AG},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AG", "BG"] },
            { text: "and twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB} with the rectangle {AG} by {GB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AG", "BG"] },
            { text: "therefore the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB} is incommensurable with twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AG", "BG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "sum incommensurable with twice rectangle", ref: "X.13" }] },
            { text: "But {CL} equals the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CL"] },
            { text: "and {FL} equals twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FL"] },
            { text: "therefore {CL} is also incommensurable with {FL}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CL", "FL"] },
            { text: "But {CL} is to {FL} as {CM} is to {FM}, therefore {CM} is incommensurable in length with {FM}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CL", "FL", "CM", "FM"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CL : FL = CM : FM", ref: "VI.1" }] },
            { text: "And both are rational, therefore {CM} and {MF} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CM", "FM"] },
            { text: "therefore {CF} is an apotome.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CF"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CF an apotome", ref: "X.73" }] },
            { text: "I say next that it is also a third apotome.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CF"] },
            { text: "Since the square on {AG} is commensurable with the square on {GB}, therefore {CH} is also commensurable with {KL},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AG", "BG", "CH", "KL"] },
            { text: "so that {CK} is also commensurable with {KM}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CK", "KM"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CH : KL = CK : KM", ref: "VI.1" }, { ref: "X.11" }] },
            { text: "Since the rectangle {AG} by {GB} is a mean proportional between the squares on {AG} and {GB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AG", "BG"] },
            { text: "{CH} equals the square on {AG}, {KL} equals the square on {GB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CH", "KL"] },
            { text: "and {NL} equals the rectangle {AG} by {GB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["NL"] },
            { text: "therefore {NL} is also a mean proportional between {CH} and {KL}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["NL", "CH", "KL"] },
            { text: "Therefore {CH} is to {NL} as {NL} is to {KL}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CH", "NL", "KL"] },
            { text: "But {CH} is to {NL} as {CK} is to {NM},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CK", "MN"] },
            { text: "and {NL} is to {KL} as {NM} is to {KM},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["MN", "KM"] },
            { text: "therefore {CK} is to {MN} as {MN} is to {KM}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CK", "MN", "KM"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "VI.1" }, { ref: "V.11" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the rectangle {CK} by {KM} equals the square on {MN},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CK", "KM", "MN"] },
            { text: "that is, to the fourth part of the square on {FM}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FM"] },
            { text: "Since, then, {CM} and {MF} are two unequal straight lines,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CM", "FM"] },
            { text: "and a parallelogram equal to the fourth part of the square on {FM} and deficient by a square figure",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FM"] },
            { text: "has been applied to {CM}, and divides it into commensurable parts,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CK", "KM"] },
            { text: "therefore the square on {CM} is greater than the square on {MF}",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CM", "FM"] },
            { text: "by the square on a straight line commensurable with {CM}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CM"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "X.17" }] },
            { text: "And neither of the straight lines {CM} nor {MF} is commensurable in length",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CM", "FM"] },
            { text: "with the rational straight line {CD} set out,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CD"] },
            { text: "therefore {CF} is a third apotome.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CF"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "third apotome", ref: "X.Def.III.3" }] },
            { text: "Therefore, the square on a second apotome of a medial straight line applied to a rational straight line",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB", "CD", "CE"] },
            { text: "produces as breadth a third apotome.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CF"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "X.99") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "II.7":        "/elements/books/bookII/propositions/propII7/",
        "V.11":        "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV11/",
        "VI.1":        "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI1/",
        "X.11":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX11/",
        "X.13":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX13/",
        "X.15":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX15/",
        "X.17":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX17/",
        "X.22":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX22/",
        "X.23.Cor":    "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX23/#cor",
        "X.73":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX73/",
        "X.75":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX75/",
        "X.Def.III.3": "/elements/books/bookX/definitions/defX.III.3/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Apply {CH}, equal to the square on {AG}, to {CD} producing {CK} as breadth, and apply {KL}, equal to the square on {BG}, to {KH} producing {KM} as breadth. Then the whole {CL} equals the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB}. Therefore {CL} is also medial. [!just X.15; X.23.Cor]

And it is applied to the rational straight line {CD} producing {CM} as breadth, therefore {CM} is rational and incommensurable in length with {CD}. [!just X.22]

Now, since the whole {CL} equals the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB}, and, in these, {CE} equals the square on {AB}, therefore the remainder {LF} equals twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB}. [!just II.7]

Bisect {FM} at the point {N}, and draw {NO} parallel to {CD}. Then each of the rectangles {FO} and {NL} equals the rectangle {AG} by {GB}.

But the rectangle {AG} by {GB} is medial, therefore {FL} is also medial.

And it is applied to the rational straight line {EF} producing {FM} as breadth, therefore {FM} is also rational and incommensurable in length with {CD}. [!just X.22]

Since {AG} and {GB} are commensurable in square only, therefore {AG} is incommensurable in length with {GB}. Therefore the square on {AG} is also incommensurable with the rectangle {AG} by {GB}. [!just VI.1; X.11]

But the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB} is commensurable with the square on {AG}, and twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB} with the rectangle {AG} by {GB}, therefore the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB} is incommensurable with twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB}. [!just X.13]

But {CL} equals the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB}, and {FL} equals twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB}, therefore {CL} is also incommensurable with {FL}.

But {CL} is to {FL} as {CM} is to {FM}, therefore {CM} is incommensurable in length with {FM}. [!just VI.1]

And both are rational, therefore {CM} and {MF} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only, therefore {CF} is an apotome. [!just X.73]

I say next that it is also a third apotome.

Since the square on {AG} is commensurable with the square on {GB}, therefore {CH} is also commensurable with {KL}, so that {CK} is also commensurable with {KM}. [!just VI.1, X.11]

Since the rectangle {AG} by {GB} is a mean proportional between the squares on {AG} and {GB}, {CH} equals the square on {AG}, {KL} equals the square on {GB}, and {NL} equals the rectangle {AG} by {GB}, therefore {NL} is also a mean proportional between {CH} and {KL}. Therefore {CH} is to {NL} as {NL} is to {KL}.

But {CH} is to {NL} as {CK} is to {NM}, and {NL} is to {KL} as {NM} is to {KM}, therefore {CK} is to {MN} as {MN} is to {KM}. Therefore the rectangle {CK} by {KM} equals the square on {MN}, that is, to the fourth part of the square on {FM}. [!just VI.1; V.11]

Since, then, {CM} and {MF} are two unequal straight lines, and a parallelogram equal to the fourth part of the square on {FM} and deficient by a square figure has been applied to {CM}, and divides it into commensurable parts, therefore the square on {CM} is greater than the square on {MF} by the square on a straight line commensurable with {CM}. [!just X.17]

And neither of the straight lines {CM} nor {MF} is commensurable in length with the rational straight line {CD} set out, therefore {CF} is a third apotome. [!just X.Def.III.3]

Therefore, *the square on a second apotome of a medial straight line applied to a rational straight line produces as breadth a third apotome.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
